## Formula Dream boundaries

Never:

- list Formula Neon as the employer;
- split the integrated work into invented employers;
- attribute the Formula Neon main account's growth to Lohith;
- move Formulytics metrics to another employer or a future project;
- claim exact revenue, conversion, retention, uptime, error rate, or time savings not recorded here;
- describe the role as only content creation;
- restore any deleted legacy evidence;
- relabel the role's primary scaling stage as 1-to-10.

## Think Round boundaries

Never claim:

- mental-health board approval;
- clinical efficacy, diagnosis, treatment, or replacement of therapy;
- production launch, adoption, user counts, health outcomes, or exact latency;
- that unfinished agents were launched;
- an unconfirmed regeneration or retry design;
- an `Intern`, `Prompt Engineer`, or `Team Lead` title;
- two separate Think Round jobs;
- any deleted non-AI work from an older canonical.

Reference contact recorded for verification use only, not default resume display: Heidi, heidi@thinkround.org.

## Cognizant boundaries

Never claim:

- an exact infrastructure-cost reduction;
- a certification, duration, platform-specific metric, or new business outcome that is not supported;
- later employer metrics, products, or responsibilities as Cognizant work;
- an unconfirmed team size, business domain, client, dashboard count, uptime, or error rate;
- a title other than Program Analyst.
